            <ArticleTitle>[Between filiation and affiliation, constructing an identity through drawing in anorexia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1259-4792(16)30133-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.spp.2016.11.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Claire, a French-Korean teenager suffering from anorexia, favours drawing as a means of self-expression. Her graphic creations illustrate the search for identity of this child of migrants. Struggling with an impossible identification linked to her filiation, drawing represents for her a real object of mediation. It gives meaning to what dwells within her and constitutes the medium of her creativity.</AbstractText>
